# AI Native Application Server

```text
Cliente -> Rust (API + backend tradicional)
              └─ use case agentic? -> Mojo runtime -> Python agent contract
```

Rust is the only public process. Clients must never call Mojo directly.

## Process split

| Process | Path | Owns | Must not do |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Rust application server | `src/**/*.rs` | public HTTP, CRUD, DBs, auth, request control | agent graph, RAG, harness |
| Mojo agent runtime | `ai-agent-runtime/**/*.mojo` | embedded CPython lifecycle, module/object cache, private HTTP/IPC, execution | reimplementing contract behavior |
| Python agent contract | `ai-agent-contract/src/ai_orchestrator/` | agent, graph, use-case and adapter definitions | public ingress, traditional CRUD |

Not every request uses the agentic stack. A Rust use case invokes the private
Mojo runtime only when the flow needs an agent. Mojo eagerly loads and caches
the Python contract, then executes its composition root in-process.

Mojo must use `Python.import_module()` and the CPython embedding variables
`MOJO_PYTHON` and `MOJO_PYTHON_LIBRARY`. Never spawn Python as a subprocess.

## Ownership

| Layer | Path | Owns | Must not do |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Rust application | `src/application/`, `src/ports/` | public business use cases and internal agent port | Python orchestration |
| Rust adapters | `src/infrastructure/`, `src/transport/` | data adapters, private Mojo client, public API | agent implementation |
| Mojo runtime | `ai-agent-runtime/src/` | CPython interop, mirrored loaders, object registry and private transport | duplicated contract logic |
| Python contract | `ai-agent-contract/src/ai_orchestrator/` | domain, use cases, orchestration, adapters, composition root | public client API |

Do not create a second Mojo `Agent`, graph, RAG, or use-case implementation.
Every Python module must have a homologous generated loader under
`ai-agent-runtime/src/contracts/`; extend the Python contract and regenerate
the loaders.

vLLM / LiteLLM stay as external HTTP services. Training/HF serving stay out of both processes.

## Placement rule

- Traditional backend feature → Rust, state the layer.
- Agent / RAG / harness definition → Python `ai-agent-contract`, state the layer.
- Runtime, cache, CPython lifecycle, or private transport → Mojo `ai-agent-runtime`.

```mojo
var api = Python.import_module("ai_orchestrator.host_api")
```
